## Block 1: two committed package tests cannot both pass

The Red test `packages/read-along/components/read-along/__tests__/phase3-a11y.test.tsx` line 45 asserts that a word span holds `tabindex="0"`:

```tsx
const word = getByText("small");
expect(word).toHaveAttribute("tabindex", "0");
```

The committed package test `packages/read-along/components/read-along/__tests__/read-along-passage.test.tsx` line 190 asserts that the same render holds exactly one `[tabindex='0']` element, and that element is the sentence:

```tsx
expect(container.querySelectorAll("[tabindex='0']")).toHaveLength(1);
expect(container.querySelectorAll("[role='button']")).toHaveLength(1);
const stop = container.querySelector("[data-sentence='0']") as HTMLElement;
expect(stop).toHaveAttribute("tabindex", "0");
```

Both tests render `ReadAlongPassage` with `active` and `onWordTap`. The Red test needs at least two focusable elements. The older test allows exactly one. No implementation can satisfy both. Green may not edit a committed Red test. The task brief also requires every existing package test to pass.

The code graph shows the conflict sits in the package that Primary also ships. Primary keeps its own copy, so the older test is the package contract.

## Block 2: the Red route test needs client code in the server page

The Red app test `apps/storytime/__tests__/phase3-readalong-ui.test.tsx` reads only `app/[locale]/st/[level]/[week]/page.tsx` as text. It requires these client-only markers in that file:

- `play()`.
- `onError` or `addEventListener("error")`.
- `playbackRate = 1`.
- `touchStart` or `onTouchStart`.
- `play()`, `pause()`, `ArrowLeft`, `ArrowRight`, `slowFile`, and `slowSentences`.

That file is the server gate. It holds `export const dynamic = "force-dynamic"`, `generateMetadata()` with `noindex`, `loadVisibleWeek`, and `notFound()`. The committed tests `phase3-entry-route.test.ts` and `phase3-home-card.test.tsx` also read that file for those server markers. An App Router page file cannot be a client component and keep the server gate. Event handlers and refs in a server component fail the build.

So the Red route test cannot pass without either a Mid Red retarget to a client component file, or source-only text that does not run. Green rejects the second option as fabrication.

